{"id":"dudoan-01","section":4,"path":"bank/listening/dudoan-01/audio-4.mp3","model":"small","duration":1034.27,"segments":[{"start":0.0,"end":5.64,"text":"Section 4 You will hear part of a linguistics lecture about","words":[["Section",0.0,0.62],["4",0.62,1.14],["You",1.14,2.8],["will",2.8,3.0],["hear",3.0,3.26],["part",3.26,3.62],["of",3.62,3.76],["a",3.76,3.88],["linguistics",3.88,4.52],["lecture",4.52,5.04],["about",5.04,5.64]]},{"start":5.64,"end":12.94,"text":"a language called Bishlama that is spoken in the Pacific Islands. First you have some","words":[["a",5.64,5.88],["language",5.88,6.34],["called",6.34,6.94],["Bishlama",6.94,8.0],["that",8.0,8.78],["is",8.78,8.9],["spoken",8.9,9.24],["in",9.24,9.7],["the",9.7,9.84],["Pacific",9.84,10.18],["Islands.",10.18,10.76],["First",11.72,12.32],["you",12.32,12.6],["have",12.6,12.76],["some",12.76,12.94]]},{"start":12.94,"end":71.85,"text":"time to look at questions 31-40 on page 7. Now listen carefully and answer questions 31-40.","words":[["time",12.94,13.36],["to",13.36,13.62],["look",13.62,13.78],["at",13.78,13.9],["questions",13.9,14.24],["31",14.24,15.0],["-40",15.0,15.72],["on",15.72,16.44],["page",16.44,16.72],["7.",16.72,17.22],["Now",67.87,68.25],["listen",68.25,68.63],["carefully",68.63,69.09],["and",69.09,69.47],["answer",69.47,69.97],["questions",69.97,70.35],["31",70.35,71.25],["-40.",71.25,71.85]]},{"start":75.29,"end":80.39,"text":"Good morning and welcome back to this series of linguistics lectures. Today I will be","words":[["Good",75.29,75.73],["morning",75.73,76.05],["and",76.05,76.29],["welcome",76.29,76.61],["back",76.61,76.89],["to",76.89,77.03],["this",77.03,77.17],["series",77.17,77.47],["of",77.47,77.67],["linguistics",77.67,78.17],["lectures.",78.17,78.55],["Today",79.27,79.61],["I",79.61,80.17],["will",80.17,80.29],["be",80.29,80.39]]},{"start":80.39,"end":84.25,"text":"talking about the language Bishlama which is a form of Pigeon English.","words":[["talking",80.39,80.61],["about",80.61,80.89],["the",80.89,81.01],["language",81.01,81.33],["Bishlama",81.33,82.23],["which",82.23,82.81],["is",82.81,82.95],["a",82.95,83.05],["form",83.05,83.35],["of",83.35,83.55],["Pigeon",83.55,83.97],["English.",83.97,84.25]]},{"start":85.05,"end":89.91,"text":"Linguists use the term Pigeon to describe new languages that are created by combining","words":[["Linguists",85.05,85.59],["use",85.59,85.91],["the",85.91,86.05],["term",86.05,86.29],["Pigeon",86.29,86.89],["to",86.89,87.29],["describe",87.29,87.63],["new",87.63,87.95],["languages",87.95,88.37],["that",88.37,88.65],["are",88.65,88.75],["created",88.75,89.17],["by",89.17,89.47],["combining",89.47,89.91]]},{"start":89.91,"end":93.57,"text":"two or more existing languages, often in a simplified form.","words":[["two",89.91,90.35],["or",90.35,90.59],["more",90.59,90.87],["existing",90.87,91.33],["languages,",91.33,91.85],["often",92.15,92.49],["in",92.49,92.63],["a",92.63,92.77],["simplified",92.77,93.07],["form.",93.07,93.57]]},{"start":94.49,"end":98.79,"text":"The study of Pigeon languages is important because it provides us with information about","words":[["The",94.49,94.65],["study",94.65,94.93],["of",94.93,95.09],["Pigeon",95.09,95.45],["languages",95.45,95.83],["is",95.83,96.11],["important",96.11,96.63],["because",96.63,96.97],["it",96.97,97.11],["provides",97.11,97.49],["us",97.49,97.67],["with",97.67,97.83],["information",97.83,98.33],["about",98.33,98.79]]},{"start":98.79,"end":100.49,"text":"language change and modification.","words":[["language",98.79,99.23],["change",99.23,99.69],["and",99.69,100.03],["modification.",100.03,100.49]]},{"start":101.91,"end":106.65,"text":"The Pigeon English known as Bishlama is used in the South Pacific nation of Vanuatu,","words":[["The",101.91,102.23],["Pigeon",102.23,102.61],["English",102.61,102.85],["known",102.85,103.09],["as",103.09,103.25],["Bishlama",103.25,103.87],["is",103.87,104.41],["used",104.41,104.65],["in",104.65,104.81],["the",104.81,104.91],["South",104.91,105.19],["Pacific",105.19,105.39],["nation",105.39,105.85],["of",105.85,106.03],["Vanuatu,",106.03,106.65]]},{"start":106.65,"end":112.41,"text":"to, a group of islands where 81 first languages are still regularly used by the local people.","words":[["to,",106.65,106.79],["a",107.07,107.41],["group",107.41,107.63],["of",107.63,107.79],["islands",107.79,108.13],["where",108.13,108.39],["81",108.39,108.99],["first",108.99,109.49],["languages",109.49,109.95],["are",109.95,110.33],["still",110.33,110.57],["regularly",110.57,110.99],["used",110.99,111.45],["by",111.45,111.65],["the",111.65,111.79],["local",111.79,112.01],["people.",112.01,112.41]]},{"start":113.31,"end":118.29,"text":"There are a further 17 local languages that are in danger of dying out, and 8 that have","words":[["There",113.31,113.49],["are",113.49,113.61],["a",113.61,113.75],["further",113.75,113.95],["17",113.95,114.51],["local",114.51,115.11],["languages",115.11,115.67],["that",115.67,115.85],["are",115.85,115.95],["in",115.95,116.07],["danger",116.07,116.33],["of",116.33,116.49],["dying",116.49,116.79],["out,",116.79,117.07],["and",117.43,117.59],["8",117.59,117.97],["that",117.97,118.21],["have",118.21,118.29]]},{"start":118.29,"end":124.97,"text":"been identified as extinct. This gives a total of 106 first languages in all, a very high","words":[["been",118.29,118.47],["identified",118.47,119.09],["as",119.09,119.39],["extinct.",119.39,119.79],["This",120.59,120.95],["gives",120.95,121.19],["a",121.19,121.37],["total",121.37,121.63],["of",121.63,121.81],["106",121.81,122.53],["first",122.53,122.85],["languages",122.85,123.39],["in",123.39,123.65],["all,",123.65,123.89],["a",124.25,124.39],["very",124.39,124.71],["high",124.71,124.97]]},{"start":124.97,"end":128.79,"text":"number for a small country with a population of just 200,000 people.","words":[["number",124.97,125.23],["for",125.23,125.41],["a",125.41,125.53],["small",125.53,125.71],["country",125.71,126.13],["with",126.13,126.29],["a",126.29,126.39],["population",126.39,126.71],["of",126.71,127.11],["just",127.11,127.29],["200",127.29,127.73],[",000",127.73,128.37],["people.",128.37,128.79]]},{"start":129.81,"end":135.15,"text":"Then thinking about foreign languages, English is the most important and has official status,","words":[["Then",129.81,130.29],["thinking",130.29,130.59],["about",130.59,130.89],["foreign",130.89,131.23],["languages,",131.23,131.77],["English",132.35,132.65],["is",132.65,132.91],["the",132.91,133.05],["most",133.05,133.33],["important",133.33,133.79],["and",133.79,134.07],["has",134.07,134.27],["official",134.27,134.65],["status,",134.65,135.15]]},{"start":135.15,"end":138.91,"text":"largely because it is the medium for all education purposes.","words":[["largely",135.15,135.89],["because",135.89,136.35],["it",136.35,136.49],["is",136.49,136.63],["the",136.63,136.77],["medium",136.77,137.09],["for",137.09,137.35],["all",137.35,137.67],["education",137.67,138.21],["purposes.",138.21,138.91]]},{"start":139.93,"end":144.59,"text":"However, it is Bishlama that is the most widely spoken language in the country,","words":[["However,",139.93,140.55],["it",141.15,141.29],["is",141.29,141.41],["Bishlama",141.41,142.01],["that",142.01,142.23],["is",142.23,142.41],["the",142.41,142.55],["most",142.55,142.73],["widely",142.73,143.15],["spoken",143.15,143.53],["language",143.53,143.95],["in",143.95,144.13],["the",144.13,144.25],["country,",144.25,144.59]]},{"start":144.93,"end":147.95,"text":"used regularly by more than 90% of the population.","words":[["used",144.93,145.29],["regularly",145.29,145.71],["by",145.71,145.95],["more",145.95,146.15],["than",146.15,146.29],["90",146.29,146.69],["%",146.69,147.07],["of",147.07,147.25],["the",147.25,147.33],["population.",147.33,147.95]]},{"start":148.89,"end":153.89,"text":"We should note here that in earlier times some people had negative feelings towards the language.","words":[["We",148.89,149.33],["should",149.33,149.49],["note",149.49,149.73],["here",149.73,150.05],["that",150.05,150.45],["in",150.45,150.57],["earlier",150.57,150.87],["times",150.87,151.35],["some",151.35,151.69],["people",151.69,151.93],["had",151.93,152.15],["negative",152.15,152.51],["feelings",152.51,152.99],["towards",152.99,153.29],["the",153.29,153.57],["language.",153.57,153.89]]},{"start":154.57,"end":160.11,"text":"In fact, for many years it was commonly referred to as a broken language and its use was discouraged.","words":[["In",154.57,154.75],["fact,",154.75,155.07],["for",155.37,155.55],["many",155.55,155.85],["years",155.85,156.21],["it",156.21,156.33],["was",156.33,156.45],["commonly",156.45,156.87],["referred",156.87,157.25],["to",157.25,157.51],["as",157.51,157.71],["a",157.71,157.83],["broken",157.83,158.19],["language",158.19,158.73],["and",158.73,159.01],["its",159.01,159.15],["use",159.15,159.33],["was",159.33,159.53],["discouraged.",159.53,160.11]]},{"start":160.11,"end":165.91,"text":"But attitudes have changed dramatically and today the people of Vanuatu are very proud","words":[["But",160.11,161.05],["attitudes",161.05,161.49],["have",161.49,161.77],["changed",161.77,162.11],["dramatically",162.11,162.75],["and",162.75,163.37],["today",163.37,163.77],["the",163.77,163.93],["people",163.93,164.21],["of",164.21,164.37],["Vanuatu",164.37,164.87],["are",164.87,165.13],["very",165.13,165.51],["proud",165.51,165.91]]},{"start":165.91,"end":166.93,"text":"of this unique language.","words":[["of",165.91,166.09],["this",166.09,166.21],["unique",166.21,166.51],["language.",166.51,166.93]]},{"start":168.81,"end":173.69,"text":"It is only when we understand the historical context that we can comprehend just why Bishlama","words":[["It",168.81,169.11],["is",169.11,169.21],["only",169.21,169.45],["when",169.45,169.61],["we",169.61,169.77],["understand",169.77,170.23],["the",170.23,170.39],["historical",170.39,170.95],["context",170.95,171.49],["that",171.49,171.79],["we",171.79,171.91],["can",171.91,172.05],["comprehend",172.05,172.47],["just",172.47,172.79],["why",172.79,173.17],["Bishlama",173.17,173.69]]},{"start":173.69,"end":174.87,"text":"developed in Vanuatu.","words":[["developed",173.69,174.13],["in",174.13,174.31],["Vanuatu.",174.31,174.87]]},{"start":176.21,"end":181.11,"text":"The first form of pigeon English in this region can be traced to around 1800 when foreign","words":[["The",176.21,176.37],["first",176.37,176.61],["form",176.61,176.87],["of",176.87,177.01],["pigeon",177.01,177.19],["English",177.19,177.49],["in",177.49,177.73],["this",177.73,177.87],["region",177.87,178.19],["can",178.19,178.41],["be",178.41,178.55],["traced",178.55,178.83],["to",178.83,178.99],["around",178.99,179.27],["1800",179.27,180.05],["when",180.05,180.77],["foreign",180.77,181.11]]},{"start":181.11,"end":184.25,"text":"traders arrived and local people were recruited to work as sailors.","words":[["traders",181.11,181.51],["arrived",181.51,181.91],["and",181.91,182.15],["local",182.15,182.43],["people",182.43,182.77],["were",182.77,182.95],["recruited",182.95,183.33],["to",183.33,183.55],["work",183.55,183.73],["as",183.73,183.93],["sailors.",183.93,184.25]]},{"start":185.15,"end":191.15,"text":"On board multilingual ships, there was an obvious need for a common tongue and Pigeon English was born.","words":[["On",185.15,185.75],["board",185.75,186.01],["multilingual",186.01,186.67],["ships,",186.67,187.13],["there",187.69,187.81],["was",187.81,187.93],["an",187.93,188.05],["obvious",188.05,188.37],["need",188.37,188.69],["for",188.69,188.87],["a",188.87,189.05],["common",189.05,189.27],["tongue",189.27,189.63],["and",189.63,190.01],["Pigeon",190.01,190.39],["English",190.39,190.59],["was",190.59,190.85],["born.",190.85,191.15]]},{"start":191.97,"end":198.55,"text":"This early former Bishlama continued to spread as trade in the Pacific developed in Sandalwood and other local commodities.","words":[["This",191.97,192.19],["early",192.19,192.59],["former",192.59,192.87],["Bishlama",192.87,193.31],["continued",193.31,194.01],["to",194.01,194.25],["spread",194.25,194.59],["as",194.59,194.89],["trade",194.89,195.21],["in",195.21,195.35],["the",195.35,195.43],["Pacific",195.43,195.73],["developed",195.73,196.23],["in",196.23,196.43],["Sandalwood",196.43,197.05],["and",197.05,197.43],["other",197.43,197.75],["local",197.75,198.03],["commodities.",198.03,198.55]]},{"start":199.55,"end":207.01,"text":"Then from about 1860 a lot of people from Vanuatu travelled to Australia to work on the new plantations as labourers.","words":[["Then",199.55,199.83],["from",199.83,200.01],["about",200.01,200.31],["1860",200.31,201.21],["a",201.21,201.69],["lot",201.69,201.95],["of",201.95,202.07],["people",202.07,202.25],["from",202.25,202.51],["Vanuatu",202.51,203.15],["travelled",203.15,203.67],["to",203.67,203.95],["Australia",203.95,204.41],["to",204.41,204.75],["work",204.75,204.97],["on",204.97,205.19],["the",205.19,205.29],["new",205.29,205.47],["plantations",205.47,206.13],["as",206.13,206.41],["labourers.",206.41,207.01]]},{"start":207.63,"end":213.85,"text":"Again, because of the multilingual nature of these workplaces, it was very important to have a common language.","words":[["Again,",207.63,207.99],["because",208.43,208.77],["of",208.77,208.99],["the",208.99,209.09],["multilingual",209.09,209.77],["nature",209.77,210.13],["of",210.13,210.37],["these",210.37,210.51],["workplaces,",210.51,211.21],["it",211.69,211.83],["was",211.83,211.97],["very",211.97,212.33],["important",212.33,212.75],["to",212.75,212.93],["have",212.93,213.07],["a",213.07,213.17],["common",213.17,213.41],["language.",213.41,213.85]]},{"start":213.85,"end":217.33,"text":"language. Finally, in modern times, there have been","words":[["language.",213.85,213.99],["Finally,",215.05,215.61],["in",215.81,215.89],["modern",215.89,216.17],["times,",216.17,216.61],["there",216.97,217.07],["have",217.07,217.15],["been",217.15,217.33]]},{"start":217.33,"end":219.97,"text":"other pressures that have maintained the need for a common language.","words":[["other",217.33,217.65],["pressures",217.65,218.03],["that",218.03,218.25],["have",218.25,218.35],["maintained",218.35,218.63],["the",218.63,218.89],["need",218.89,219.07],["for",219.07,219.21],["a",219.21,219.35],["common",219.35,219.55],["language.",219.55,219.97]]},{"start":220.89,"end":226.53,"text":"Like many other parts of the world, from about the 1950s, Vanuatu experienced a significant","words":[["Like",220.89,221.11],["many",221.11,221.45],["other",221.45,221.65],["parts",221.65,221.93],["of",221.93,222.09],["the",222.09,222.17],["world,",222.17,222.43],["from",222.69,222.69],["about",222.69,222.97],["the",222.97,223.11],["1950s,",223.11,224.55],["Vanuatu",224.85,225.27],["experienced",225.27,225.87],["a",225.87,226.05],["significant",226.05,226.53]]},{"start":226.53,"end":231.25,"text":"migration of its people from small villages into the city and it has been here that","words":[["migration",226.53,227.03],["of",227.03,227.37],["its",227.37,227.47],["people",227.47,227.77],["from",227.77,227.99],["small",227.99,228.39],["villages",228.39,228.77],["into",228.77,229.19],["the",229.19,229.37],["city",229.37,229.61],["and",229.61,230.23],["it",230.23,230.33],["has",230.33,230.47],["been",230.47,230.67],["here",230.67,231.03],["that",231.03,231.25]]},{"start":231.25,"end":235.15,"text":"Bishlama has really established itself as the country's first language.","words":[["Bishlama",231.25,231.73],["has",231.73,232.05],["really",232.05,232.47],["established",232.47,233.01],["itself",233.01,233.49],["as",233.49,233.75],["the",233.75,233.87],["country's",233.87,234.37],["first",234.37,234.61],["language.",234.61,235.15]]},{"start":240.28,"end":246.06,"text":"So then, how can we describe the language itself? In general terms, pigeon languages","words":[["So",240.28,240.66],["then,",240.66,240.84],["how",241.3,241.54],["can",241.54,241.7],["we",241.7,241.8],["describe",241.8,242.14],["the",242.14,242.3],["language",242.3,242.62],["itself?",242.62,243.04],["In",243.8,244.14],["general",244.14,244.5],["terms,",244.5,244.9],["pigeon",245.4,245.64],["languages",245.64,246.06]]},{"start":246.06,"end":251.3,"text":"languages can be defined as extremely simple versions of the original language. However,","words":[["languages",246.06,246.24],["can",246.24,246.44],["be",246.44,246.56],["defined",246.56,246.88],["as",246.88,247.16],["extremely",247.16,247.8],["simple",247.8,248.32],["versions",248.32,248.84],["of",248.84,249.12],["the",249.12,249.24],["original",249.24,249.62],["language.",249.62,250.14],["However,",250.98,251.3]]},{"start":251.84,"end":256.84,"text":"this is not a satisfactory definition in this case, and linguists prefer to describe Bishlama","words":[["this",251.84,251.94],["is",251.94,252.08],["not",252.08,252.38],["a",252.38,252.56],["satisfactory",252.56,253.04],["definition",253.04,253.7],["in",253.7,253.94],["this",253.94,254.12],["case,",254.12,254.42],["and",254.6,254.78],["linguists",254.78,255.22],["prefer",255.22,255.7],["to",255.7,256.0],["describe",256.0,256.38],["Bishlama",256.38,256.84]]},{"start":256.84,"end":263.26,"text":"as a developed pigeon, because it has more rules and ideas than most simple pigeon languages","words":[["as",256.84,257.34],["a",257.34,257.62],["developed",257.62,258.5],["pigeon,",258.5,259.12],["because",259.54,259.94],["it",259.94,260.1],["has",260.1,260.26],["more",260.26,260.54],["rules",260.54,260.88],["and",260.88,261.04],["ideas",261.04,261.42],["than",261.42,261.66],["most",261.66,262.02],["simple",262.02,262.44],["pigeon",262.44,262.74],["languages",262.74,263.26]]},{"start":263.26,"end":268.44,"text":"found in other parts of the world. Let's think first about the vocabulary.","words":[["found",263.26,263.84],["in",263.84,264.04],["other",264.04,264.18],["parts",264.18,264.5],["of",264.5,264.64],["the",264.64,264.72],["world.",264.72,265.02],["Let's",266.42,267.1],["think",267.1,267.26],["first",267.26,267.58],["about",267.58,267.92],["the",267.92,268.04],["vocabulary.",268.04,268.44]]},{"start":269.3,"end":274.22,"text":"Because Britain was the colonial power, the majority of Bishlama's vocabulary is","words":[["Because",269.3,269.68],["Britain",269.68,270.04],["was",270.04,270.22],["the",270.22,270.38],["colonial",270.38,270.78],["power,",270.78,271.28],["the",271.78,271.88],["majority",271.88,272.3],["of",272.3,272.64],["Bishlama's",272.64,273.3],["vocabulary",273.3,273.84],["is",273.84,274.22]]},{"start":274.22,"end":282.12,"text":"derived from English. However, some care needs to be taken here. For example, the word from","words":[["derived",274.22,274.58],["from",274.58,274.88],["English.",274.88,275.3],["However,",276.26,276.7],["some",277.24,277.5],["care",277.5,277.8],["needs",277.8,278.06],["to",278.06,278.26],["be",278.26,278.34],["taken",278.34,278.64],["here.",278.64,278.94],["For",279.8,280.04],["example,",280.04,280.46],["the",281.06,281.16],["word",281.16,281.46],["from",281.46,282.12]]},{"start":282.12,"end":288.72,"text":"in Bishlama can also mean because of, so we need to be aware that words can have a wider","words":[["in",282.12,282.7],["Bishlama",282.7,283.2],["can",283.2,283.56],["also",283.56,283.8],["mean",283.8,284.18],["because",284.18,285.08],["of,",285.08,285.66],["so",286.3,286.58],["we",286.58,286.7],["need",286.7,286.92],["to",286.92,287.08],["be",287.08,287.2],["aware",287.2,287.46],["that",287.46,287.62],["words",287.62,287.84],["can",287.84,288.1],["have",288.1,288.3],["a",288.3,288.38],["wider",288.38,288.72]]},{"start":288.72,"end":294.84,"text":"range of meanings in Bishlama. Indeed, there are numerous other potentially misleading terms","words":[["range",288.72,289.04],["of",289.04,289.18],["meanings",289.18,289.5],["in",289.5,289.84],["Bishlama.",289.84,290.36],["Indeed,",291.3,291.64],["there",292.06,292.26],["are",292.26,292.38],["numerous",292.38,292.84],["other",292.84,293.26],["potentially",293.26,293.92],["misleading",293.92,294.38],["terms",294.38,294.84]]},{"start":294.84,"end":298.06,"text":"and English is not the only contributor to the vocabulary.","words":[["and",294.84,295.42],["English",295.42,295.76],["is",295.76,295.98],["not",295.98,296.22],["the",296.22,296.4],["only",296.4,296.68],["contributor",296.68,297.16],["to",297.16,297.44],["the",297.44,297.56],["vocabulary.",297.56,298.06]]},{"start":299.4,"end":305.44,"text":"Again, because of the region's history there are some words, around 5-10%, that are derived","words":[["Again,",299.4,300.02],["because",300.6,300.96],["of",300.96,301.1],["the",301.1,301.18],["region's",301.18,301.58],["history",301.58,301.92],["there",301.92,302.08],["are",302.08,302.28],["some",302.28,302.52],["words,",302.52,302.82],["around",303.26,303.58],["5",303.58,303.92],["-10%,",303.92,304.6],["that",304.6,305.0],["are",305.0,305.1],["derived",305.1,305.44]]},{"start":305.44,"end":306.2,"text":"from French.","words":[["from",305.44,305.74],["French.",305.74,306.2]]},{"start":307.28,"end":311.94,"text":"Then a relatively small number of words have been taken from local, Pacific languages.","words":[["Then",307.28,307.62],["a",307.62,308.06],["relatively",308.06,308.46],["small",308.46,308.88],["number",308.88,309.2],["of",309.2,309.38],["words",309.38,309.62],["have",309.62,309.84],["been",309.84,310.0],["taken",310.0,310.28],["from",310.28,310.52],["local,",310.52,310.9],["Pacific",311.14,311.42],["languages.",311.42,311.94]]},{"start":313.02,"end":316.82,"text":"Usually this is the case where there is no English equivalent for naturally occurring","words":[["Usually",313.02,313.44],["this",313.44,313.72],["is",313.72,313.86],["the",313.86,313.98],["case",313.98,314.22],["where",314.22,314.44],["there",314.44,314.56],["is",314.56,314.7],["no",314.7,314.94],["English",314.94,315.22],["equivalent",315.22,315.7],["for",315.7,315.96],["naturally",315.96,316.38],["occurring",316.38,316.82]]},{"start":316.82,"end":321.4,"text":"phenomena or to describe some aspect of the culture that is unique to the country.","words":[["phenomena",316.82,317.26],["or",317.26,318.1],["to",318.1,318.2],["describe",318.2,318.52],["some",318.52,318.8],["aspect",318.8,319.18],["of",319.18,319.4],["the",319.4,319.54],["culture",319.54,319.9],["that",319.9,320.12],["is",320.12,320.28],["unique",320.28,320.7],["to",320.7,320.96],["the",320.96,321.08],["country.",321.08,321.4]]},{"start":323.36,"end":325.14,"text":"Finally, a word about grammar.","words":[["Finally,",323.36,323.86],["a",324.24,324.4],["word",324.4,324.56],["about",324.56,324.8],["grammar.",324.8,325.14]]},{"start":325.14,"end":330.24,"text":"Although the vocabulary is based largely on English, it's important to note that the","words":[["Although",325.14,326.2],["the",326.2,326.42],["vocabulary",326.42,326.9],["is",326.9,327.2],["based",327.2,327.44],["largely",327.44,327.94],["on",327.94,328.12],["English,",328.12,328.36],["it's",328.92,329.14],["important",329.14,329.56],["to",329.56,329.78],["note",329.78,329.98],["that",329.98,330.14],["the",330.14,330.24]]},{"start":330.24,"end":335.14,"text":"grammatical structure of Bishlama is derived from patterns common in the local languages","words":[["grammatical",330.24,330.9],["structure",330.9,331.34],["of",331.34,331.54],["Bishlama",331.54,331.96],["is",331.96,332.36],["derived",332.36,332.72],["from",332.72,333.0],["patterns",333.0,333.38],["common",333.38,333.94],["in",333.94,334.22],["the",334.22,334.32],["local",334.32,334.6],["languages",334.6,335.14]]},{"start":335.14,"end":335.94,"text":"of Vanuatu.","words":[["of",335.14,335.36],["Vanuatu.",335.36,335.94]]},{"start":336.74,"end":340.86,"text":"So for example there are two distinct pronouns meaning we.","words":[["So",336.74,337.28],["for",337.28,337.68],["example",337.68,338.0],["there",338.0,338.22],["are",338.22,338.34],["two",338.34,338.64],["distinct",338.64,339.18],["pronouns",339.18,339.74],["meaning",339.74,340.24],["we.",340.24,340.86]]},{"start":341.6,"end":347.68,"text":"One means I and you, and another means I and some others but not you.","words":[["One",341.6,341.84],["means",341.84,342.2],["I",342.2,342.82],["and",342.82,343.16],["you,",343.16,343.44],["and",344.12,344.32],["another",344.32,344.56],["means",344.56,344.9],["I",344.9,345.64],["and",345.64,345.94],["some",345.94,346.28],["others",346.28,346.58],["but",346.58,347.08],["not",347.08,347.36],["you.",347.36,347.68]]},{"start":348.62,"end":353.46,"text":"Sounds confusing in English but in the local languages such distinctions are common.","words":[["Sounds",348.62,349.14],["confusing",349.14,349.58],["in",349.58,349.82],["English",349.82,350.06],["but",350.06,350.5],["in",350.5,350.62],["the",350.62,350.72],["local",350.72,351.0],["languages",351.0,351.56],["such",351.56,352.18],["distinctions",352.18,352.8],["are",352.8,353.12],["common.",353.12,353.46]]},{"start":354.08,"end":360.3,"text":"A different example concerns the word long. It is almost the only preposition in Bishlama","words":[["A",354.08,354.6],["different",354.6,354.96],["example",354.96,355.48],["concerns",355.48,355.88],["the",355.88,356.18],["word",356.18,356.44],["long.",356.44,357.12],["It",357.88,358.1],["is",358.1,358.2],["almost",358.2,358.44],["the",358.44,358.66],["only",358.66,359.02],["preposition",359.02,359.6],["in",359.6,359.84],["Bishlama",359.84,360.3]]},{"start":360.3,"end":367.62,"text":"and may be used in place of a whole range of English words such as at, to, with, on, in","words":[["and",360.3,360.62],["may",360.62,360.82],["be",360.82,360.94],["used",360.94,361.14],["in",361.14,361.28],["place",361.28,361.54],["of",361.54,361.72],["a",361.72,361.8],["whole",361.8,362.06],["range",362.06,362.34],["of",362.34,362.5],["English",362.5,362.7],["words",362.7,363.12],["such",363.12,363.42],["as",363.42,363.58],["at,",363.58,364.02],["to,",364.52,364.84],["with,",365.44,365.74],["on,",366.4,366.74],["in",367.38,367.62]]},{"start":367.62,"end":373.44,"text":"and so on. Well that is the end of the formal part of the lecture. If you have any questions","words":[["and",367.62,368.18],["so",368.18,368.46],["on.",368.46,368.66],["Well",370.08,370.38],["that",370.38,370.64],["is",370.64,370.74],["the",370.74,370.86],["end",370.86,370.96],["of",370.96,371.06],["the",371.06,371.12],["formal",371.12,371.32],["part",371.32,371.58],["of",371.58,371.7],["the",371.7,371.76],["lecture.",371.76,372.02],["If",372.36,372.5],["you",372.5,372.6],["have",372.6,372.76],["any",372.76,373.04],["questions",373.04,373.44]]},{"start":373.44,"end":375.06,"text":"now I'll be most happy to answer.","words":[["now",373.44,373.86],["I'll",373.86,374.14],["be",374.14,374.26],["most",374.26,374.5],["happy",374.5,374.8],["to",374.8,374.92],["answer.",374.92,375.06]]},{"start":378.08,"end":414.42,"text":"That is the end of section 4. You now have half a minute to check your answers. That","words":[["That",378.08,378.6],["is",378.6,378.74],["the",378.74,378.88],["end",378.88,379.24],["of",379.24,379.42],["section",379.42,379.68],["4.",379.68,380.2],["You",380.92,381.18],["now",381.18,381.48],["have",381.48,381.8],["half",381.8,382.12],["a",382.12,382.3],["minute",382.3,382.54],["to",382.54,382.78],["check",382.78,383.1],["your",383.1,383.3],["answers.",383.3,383.72],["That",413.98,414.42]]},{"start":414.42,"end":416.12,"text":"That is the end of the listening test.","words":[["That",414.42,414.48],["is",414.48,414.58],["the",414.58,414.74],["end",414.74,415.1],["of",415.1,415.3],["the",415.3,415.4],["listening",415.4,415.66],["test.",415.66,416.12]]},{"start":416.98,"end":422.18,"text":"You now have ten minutes to transfer your answers to the listening answer sheet.","words":[["You",416.98,417.18],["now",417.18,417.46],["have",417.46,417.82],["ten",417.82,418.22],["minutes",418.22,418.66],["to",418.66,418.96],["transfer",418.96,419.54],["your",419.54,419.8],["answers",419.8,420.24],["to",420.24,420.8],["the",420.8,420.94],["listening",420.94,421.32],["answer",421.32,421.82],["sheet.",421.82,422.18]]},{"start":902.92,"end":904.48,"text":"You have two minutes left.","words":[["You",902.92,903.14],["have",903.14,903.44],["two",903.44,903.78],["minutes",903.78,904.12],["left.",904.12,904.48]]},{"start":964.68,"end":966.26,"text":"You have one minute left.","words":[["You",964.68,964.94],["have",964.94,965.22],["one",965.22,965.52],["minute",965.52,965.82],["left.",965.82,966.26]]},{"start":1026.41,"end":1030.91,"text":"Please stop writing and wait for your question booklet to be collected.","words":[["Please",1026.41,1026.83],["stop",1026.83,1027.37],["writing",1027.37,1027.89],["and",1027.89,1028.35],["wait",1028.35,1028.61],["for",1028.61,1028.85],["your",1028.85,1028.99],["question",1028.99,1029.39],["booklet",1029.39,1029.81],["to",1029.81,1030.21],["be",1030.21,1030.43],["collected.",1030.43,1030.91]]}]}